lesson: 82
title: Rows and columns
stars: 0
explain: When things stand in rows and every row is the same length, they make an array.
explain: Multiply the number of rows by the number in each row to find how many there are.
explain: 5 rows of 7 chairs make 5 × 7 = 35 chairs.
vars: a=name r=2..10 c=2..12
answer: r * c
exercise: The hall has {r} rows of chairs with {c} chairs in each row. How many chairs are in the hall?
exercise: {a} plants {r} rows of trees. Each row has {c} trees. How many trees did {a} plant?
exercise: A sheet of stamps has {r} rows and {c} columns. How many stamps are on the sheet?
exercise: The garden has {r} rows of carrots, {c} carrots in each row. How many carrots are in the garden?
exercise: {a} lines up toy cars in {r} rows of {c}. How many toy cars are there?
exercise: A box of chocolates has {r} rows with {c} chocolates in each. How many chocolates are in the box?
test: How many windows does a building have if it has {r} floors and {c} windows on each floor?
test: In the classroom the desks stand in {c} columns and {r} rows. How many desks are there?
test: {a} counts {c} tiles along each of the {r} rows of the floor. How many tiles cover the floor?
test: An egg tray holds {c} eggs in a row, and it has {r} rows. How many eggs fill the tray?
exercise: A car park in Texas has {r} rows with {c} cars in every row. How many cars are parked there?
exercise: How many chairs are in a hall with {c} chairs in each of {r} rows?
exercise: {a} sets out {r} rows of cupcakes, {c} cupcakes per row. How many cupcakes are there in all?
exercise: A choir in Wales stands in {r} rows of {c} singers. How many singers are in the choir?
exercise: The orchard in Kent has {r} rows of apple trees with {c} trees in every row. How many apple trees are there altogether?
exercise: A grid drawn by {a} has {r} rows and {c} columns of squares. How many squares are in the grid?
exercise: A small cinema in Toronto has {r} rows with {c} seats in each. How many seats does the cinema have?
exercise: {a} hangs {r} rows of photos on a wall, with {c} photos in each row. How many photos are on the wall?
test: A small plane has {r} rows of seats and {c} seats per row. How many passengers can it seat?
test: How many tiles are in a wall with {c} columns and {r} rows of tiles?
test: A box in Melbourne holds {c} muffins in each of its {r} rows. How many muffins does the box hold?
test: {a} plants {c} lettuces in a row and makes {r} such rows. How many lettuces did {a} plant?
test: In a parade in Dublin, the band marches in {r} rows, {c} players in a row. How many players are in the band?
test: A sheet of stickers is {c} stickers wide and {r} stickers long. How many stickers are on the sheet?
exercise: hall's got {r} rows, {c} chairs a row. how many chairs
exercise: {a} planted {r} rows of trees, {c} in each. how many trees {a.he} planted
exercise: stamp sheet {r+1} rows — no sorry, {r} rows — n {c} columns. how many stamps
exercise: {r} rows of {c} carrots, {a} counted one row twice n got {r*c+c}. whats the right number
test: {c} chairs in a row, {r} rows. how many chairs all up
test: garden: {r} rows, {c} cabbages each, the gate's 2 metres wide btw. how many cabbages
test: {a} reckons {r} rows of {c} seats is {r*c-c}?? not right innit. how many seats
exam: Determine the total number of chairs in an assembly hall in which {r.words} rows, each comprising {c.words} chairs, are arranged.
exam: It is given that a rectangular arrangement of tiles comprises {r} rows and {c} columns. Ascertain the number of tiles in the arrangement.
exam: State the number of trees planted by {a}, who established {r} rows of {c} trees each.
exam: Compute the number of window panes in a frame composed of {c} columns and {r} rows of panes.
exercise: In the memorial park the graves are in {r} rows, with {c} graves in each row. How many graves are there?
exercise: For Gran's celebration of life, the hall was set with {r} rows of {c} chairs. How many chairs were set out?
test: the ad said 'deceptively spacious' garden — my backside, it's tiny. fits {r} rows of {c} cabbages. how many cabbages
